+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic corpus built from the 30-word frequent vocabulary, the measured full-recall p95 before the term-selection fix was **35.53 ms**. At that point, the FTS5/BM25 query used the first 24 prompt terms.
+
+The fix selected the **eight prompt terms with the highest inverse document frequency (IDF)** before running the FTS5/BM25 query. This avoids paying for long posting lists from common, low-signal terms while retaining the most discriminating terms.
+
+After the fix, the measured full-recall p95 on the same corpus was **8.75 ms**.
+
+These are measured values from the project's `[H6]` same-corpus stage breakdown in `research/00-evidence-log.md`, not estimates.
